# A-cache across pha: pushing the same param twice loads it ONCE, then
# pushes A twice — a regression re-reads the slot before the second push.
in call_same_twice: present lda 4,s\n\tpha\n\tpha\n\tjsl add_two
count 1 lda 4,s
# A computed arg is pushed straight from A: no intermediate slot store
# between the add and the pha (dead store + A-cache pha).
in call_with_computed: present adc\.w #5\n\tpha\n\tjsl do_something
# 4-byte arg cleanup after a non-tail call is two plx, not tsa/adc/tas.
in call_same_twice: present jsl add_two\n\tplx\n\tplx\n\trtl
# The single-call wrapper needs no frame at all.
present ; Function: call_same_twice \(framesize=0,
